+### Atlas Linkage Labels (egzakta workspace, 0-N)
+
+Attach an `atlas:<node-id>` label whenever an issue maps to one or more atlas nodes (the dotted `id:` field from the node's frontmatter). Closes the reverse loop from Linear back to the atlas vault, and feeds the `org atlas drift` report.
+
+| Label form | Example | When |
+|---|---|---|
+| `atlas:<node-id>` | `atlas:capability.search.full-text-search` | Issue ships, modifies, or measures this node |
+| `atlas:<pillar-id>` | `atlas:pillar.content` | Cross-cutting issue under a pillar with no narrower node |
+
+Keep labels stable across the issue lifecycle — they survive renames in atlas filenames because they reference frontmatter `id:`, not paths.
+
